Appendix L — Open Problems (Formal Statements)

Open Problem 1 (Constructive Specification of \mathcal{M}(O)). Given an observation O and available evidence \mathcal{I}, how should the compatible model set \mathcal{M}(O) be constructed? Specifically, what are the appropriate intervals [l_i, u_i] for likelihoods and [\pi_i^L, \pi_i^U] for priors?

Open Problem 2 (Calibration Floor for User-State Inference). Does \mathcal{C}_{\text{user}} = \mathbb{E}[|P_\theta(Z = 1 \mid X) - P(Z = 1 \mid X)|] admit a non-vanishing lower bound under partial observability? If so, what is its form?

Open Problem 3 (Monotone Information Structure). Under what conditions on the user response model \Omega_R does a query guarantee \mathcal{M}_{t+1}(o) \subseteq \mathcal{M}_t for all o? When can a response expand the model set?

Open Problem 4 (Loss Parameter Elicitation). How should C_{\text{FP}}, C_{\text{FN}}, and C_q be set in deployment? What deliberative processes are appropriate for setting these parameters?

Open Problem 5 (Empirical Validation). Does the VOI criterion predict when queries are beneficial in practice? Does uncertainty contraction \Delta W_t > 0 correlate with decision quality?

Open Problem 6 (Finite-Time Calibration Floor). Given the bounded likelihood ratio condition | \log(\Pr(O \mid H_i) / \Pr(O \mid H_j)) | \leq M, what is the exact form of the finite-time lower bound g(M, \pi_{\min}, t) on W_t?

