Appendix N — Conjectures

Conjecture 1 (Finite-Time Calibration Floor). Under the bounded likelihood ratio condition, there exists a lower bound W_t \geq g(M, \pi_{\min}, t) > 0 for all finite t.

Conjecture 2 (Form of the Calibration Floor). If a lower bound on \mathcal{C}_{\text{user}} exists, it takes the form:

\inf_{\text{policy}} \mathcal{C}_{\text{user}} \geq \alpha W_t - \beta I(X; Z)

for some \alpha, \beta > 0.

Conjecture 3 (Uncertainty Contraction). For appropriately selected informative queries satisfying Assumption 2, \Delta W_t = W_t - W_{t+1} > 0.

Conjecture 4 (Decision Quality). Higher \Delta W_t predicts better decision calibration under the robust Bayes rule.

