Appendix O — Limitations

1. No empirical validation. This paper proposes a framework and an experimental protocol. It does not report experimental results.
2. Loss parameters assumed. The costs C_{\text{FP}}, C_{\text{FN}}, C_q are treated as given. Their elicitation is an open problem.
3. Operationalization of W_t imperfect. The elicitation procedure may not match the theoretical identified set.
4. State-space assumption. The POMDP formulation assumes a well-defined state space with Markovian transitions. Human wellbeing states may not satisfy this.
5. Calibration floor unproven. The existence of a non-vanishing lower bound on \mathcal{C}_{\text{user}} is conjectured, not proved.
6. Generalization uncertain. The framework is developed for a single triggering interaction. Its applicability to other contexts is an empirical question.

